      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "RIGA (4) returns for the Dilmi camp and looks to have come back in terrific order, tightening up with two sharp trial wins. He gets in well at the weights with the 2kg claimer reuniting. Bright return anticipated. ALGORITHMIC (1) finds the maiden win elusive is knocking on the door and doesn't need to improve much to finally break through. WHAT A GENT (5) has had plenty of chances but maps to get the right run and Collett taking over on the quick turnaround is a positive. He can give plenty of cheek. SPUD GUN (9) was a big improver at Hawkesbury in her third start, chasing gamely into the placings. Keeps Schofield and is open to further progress. CLASSIC TWO (2) has been better in his last two, sticking on behind dominant winners. Stays in the mix.",
